WEBVTT

00:00:23.250 --> 00:00:26.750
Miya-chan, you got it right this time!

00:00:39.410 --> 00:00:42.260
The snow feels so cool and relaxing!

00:00:44.070 --> 00:00:46.080
Yunocchi!

00:00:46.770 --> 00:00:48.650
Yunocchi!

00:00:50.010 --> 00:00:55.600
Miya-chan, you picked all the tomatoes, right?

00:00:56.190 --> 00:00:59.580
Yunocchi, it's morning!

00:00:59.580 --> 00:01:02.200
Yuno-chan really loves to sleep in!

00:01:02.200 --> 00:01:04.450
Yunocchi!

00:01:05.450 --> 00:01:07.120
Yunocchi!

00:01:13.000 --> 00:01:14.920
Morning, Yunocchi.

00:01:14.920 --> 00:01:16.010
Good morning.

00:01:16.010 --> 00:01:19.180
Huh? Miya-chan? Landlady?

00:01:19.930 --> 00:01:24.040
Yuno-chan, I won this in a raffle at the mall.

00:01:24.040 --> 00:01:24.930
You want it?

00:01:24.930 --> 00:01:27.430
She got the Game of Life Experience.

00:01:27.890 --> 00:01:29.560
Oh, um...

00:01:29.560 --> 00:01:31.770
Thank you, Landlady.

00:01:31.770 --> 00:01:35.320
People my age don't really play these kinds of things, you know?

00:01:35.320 --> 00:01:37.660
I came over to give this to you guys.

00:01:37.660 --> 00:01:41.860
I'm not surprised at all that Miyako-chan was the only one was awake, since today's a holiday.

00:01:41.860 --> 00:01:44.530
You went to all the rooms?

00:01:44.790 --> 00:01:49.400
Hey, Yunocchi, let's play the Game of Life Experience now!

00:01:49.400 --> 00:01:51.020
Oh, sure.

00:01:51.020 --> 00:01:52.460
Yay!

00:01:52.460 --> 00:01:55.500
Okay, I'll go get changed and put out some snacks.

00:01:55.500 --> 00:01:58.050
All right! I'll go get everyone else.

00:02:00.340 --> 00:02:03.360
Okay! Let's hurry so we can get started!

00:02:03.360 --> 00:02:04.720
You're playing too?!

00:02:21.610 --> 00:02:24.190
youki ni kuchibue fuite

00:02:21.610 --> 00:02:24.190
Whistling a cheerful tune

00:02:24.190 --> 00:02:26.530
madobe no kotori to sesshon

00:02:24.190 --> 00:02:26.530
I join the birds chirping by the window

00:02:26.530 --> 00:02:29.450
suima ga yatte kite

00:02:26.530 --> 00:02:29.450
When fatigue strikes

00:02:29.450 --> 00:02:32.070
atama ga danshingu

00:02:29.450 --> 00:02:32.070
My imagination runs wild

00:02:32.070 --> 00:02:34.530
nan demo kan demo waraeru nichijou

00:02:32.070 --> 00:02:34.530
Everything in life makes me smile

00:02:34.530 --> 00:02:37.370
okimari na kishoutenketsu

00:02:34.530 --> 00:02:37.370
Nothing really new takes place

00:02:37.370 --> 00:02:40.000
demo demo tama ni wa piritto supaisu

00:02:37.370 --> 00:02:40.000
But sometimes it's exciting to spice things up

00:02:40.000 --> 00:02:42.630
aozora peintingu

00:02:40.000 --> 00:02:42.630
Let's paint it on the blue sky

00:02:42.630 --> 00:02:43.670
doko ikou

00:02:42.630 --> 00:02:43.670
Where should we go?

00:02:43.670 --> 00:02:45.250
koko ni iyou

00:02:43.670 --> 00:02:45.250
Let's stay here

00:02:45.250 --> 00:02:46.250
sore wa nani

00:02:45.250 --> 00:02:46.250
What's that?

00:02:46.250 --> 00:02:47.840
are yaritai

00:02:46.250 --> 00:02:47.840
I wanna try that!

00:02:47.840 --> 00:02:50.430
ima ni tokubetsu na shirushi

00:02:47.840 --> 00:02:50.430
Let's make this moment count

00:02:50.430 --> 00:02:55.810
tokeibari no mawashikata watashi shidai kamo

00:02:50.430 --> 00:02:55.810
How fast my clock moves is all up to me

00:02:57.060 --> 00:02:59.480
shiki oriori iro toridori

00:02:57.060 --> 00:02:59.480
With a rich palette of colors from the four seasons

00:02:59.480 --> 00:03:01.940
nonbiri na everyday

00:02:59.480 --> 00:03:01.940
Our laid-back everyday lives can be

00:03:01.940 --> 00:03:04.560
pasuteru bibiddo metoro

00:03:01.940 --> 00:03:04.560
Any blend of pastel, vivid, and metro colors

00:03:04.560 --> 00:03:07.400
jibun dake no karaaringu

00:03:04.560 --> 00:03:07.400
Anyone can create their own coloring

00:03:07.400 --> 00:03:09.990
sono tokidoki mune doki doki

00:03:07.400 --> 00:03:09.990
So when your heart races in excitement

00:03:09.990 --> 00:03:13.700
hachamecha na taiyou ni oegaki

00:03:09.990 --> 00:03:13.700
Just draw a sun at the top

00:03:13.700 --> 00:03:17.830
tobidasu aatishizumu

00:03:13.700 --> 00:03:17.830
And let your inner artist take you from there

00:03:17.830 --> 00:03:21.160
gyutto shite ii kana

00:03:17.830 --> 00:03:21.160
Can I hold your hand tight?

00:03:25.920 --> 00:03:28.550
suki suki suki wo sukecchi

00:03:25.920 --> 00:03:28.550
I've been sketching everything I love

00:03:28.550 --> 00:03:31.090
nijiiro ni somete iku yo

00:03:28.550 --> 00:03:31.090
And painting them in rainbow colors

00:03:31.090 --> 00:03:35.850
sore ja ittekimasu

00:03:31.090 --> 00:03:35.850
All right, I'm off to have some more fun!

00:03:35.980 --> 00:03:40.990
November 10th, Giving Back a Smile

00:03:42.490 --> 00:03:44.990
Thank you so much, Landlady.

00:03:44.990 --> 00:03:46.280
Don't mention it.

00:03:47.120 --> 00:03:48.950
Good morning.

00:03:48.950 --> 00:03:50.870
Good morning!

00:03:50.870 --> 00:03:52.620
Hey, seniors!

00:03:52.620 --> 00:03:55.950
Landlady, what brings you here so early in the morning?

00:03:55.950 --> 00:03:59.130
I wanted to see your smiles.

00:03:59.130 --> 00:04:00.880
Oh, I remember this!

00:04:00.880 --> 00:04:02.590
It brings back memories.

00:04:02.590 --> 00:04:04.760
I think I used to play it when I was little.

00:04:04.760 --> 00:04:07.870
Do you two want to play with us too?

00:04:07.870 --> 00:04:09.910
Yeah, we have time.

00:04:09.910 --> 00:04:11.020
Yay!

00:04:11.020 --> 00:04:13.520
Shouldn't seniors be hitting the books?

00:04:13.520 --> 00:04:15.310
Sheesh, Landlady.

00:04:15.310 --> 00:04:16.790
It's just for today!

00:04:16.790 --> 00:04:20.280
Everybody needs a breather once in a while. Right?

00:04:20.820 --> 00:04:23.030
All right, let's do this.

00:04:23.680 --> 00:04:24.530
Let's see...

00:04:24.530 --> 00:04:27.270
Each person starts with 3000 dollars.

00:04:27.270 --> 00:04:30.370
So we pin the character sticks on the car pieces.

00:04:31.620 --> 00:04:35.350
I don't really get how stocks rise and fall.

00:04:35.350 --> 00:04:36.190
Huh?

00:04:36.190 --> 00:04:38.630
We've never really dealt with them.

00:04:38.630 --> 00:04:42.380
"Become a doctor" seems pretty far-fetched for us too.

00:04:42.380 --> 00:04:46.730
Landlady, mind if we change this to fit Hidamari Apartments?

00:04:46.730 --> 00:04:48.550
Oh, go ahead.

00:04:48.550 --> 00:04:50.010
Will it take much time?

00:04:50.010 --> 00:04:51.140
A little.

00:04:51.140 --> 00:04:55.050
Okay, I'm going to take a nap in Sae-chan's room. Come get me when you're done.

00:04:55.050 --> 00:04:57.400
Why does it have to be <i>my room</i>?!

00:05:00.930 --> 00:05:01.650
Here!

00:05:01.650 --> 00:05:03.370
Feel free to use these.

00:05:03.370 --> 00:05:05.130
Oh, awesome!

00:05:05.130 --> 00:05:05.990
Thanks.

00:05:05.990 --> 00:05:09.090
We can replace the events, right?

00:05:09.090 --> 00:05:13.080
You could write the new events on thick paper and tape them on.

00:05:14.640 --> 00:05:17.460
What are you painting, Yuno-san?

00:05:17.460 --> 00:05:20.710
I'm painting the car's license plate yellow

00:05:20.710 --> 00:05:23.140
to make it a light vehicle!

00:05:23.140 --> 00:05:25.450
The goal of the game is to become rich...

00:05:25.450 --> 00:05:28.550
...and you're downgrading the car?

00:05:30.560 --> 00:05:35.570
This is the first time we've all worked together since we made the Hidamari Apartments sign!

00:05:35.570 --> 00:05:37.600
I think you're right.

00:05:37.600 --> 00:05:41.810
Huh, you made that sign?

00:05:41.810 --> 00:05:43.860
Yeah, last summer.

00:05:44.180 --> 00:05:46.950
The landlady randomly asked us to.

00:05:46.950 --> 00:05:50.910
Isn't it weird? It feels like it's been much longer.

00:05:50.910 --> 00:05:52.290
Yeah.

00:05:52.290 --> 00:05:55.430
Each of us did a letter the way we wanted,

00:05:55.430 --> 00:05:58.070
so there's no real sense of uniformity.

00:05:58.070 --> 00:06:00.290
Can you tell who drew which?

00:06:02.800 --> 00:06:06.470
Oh, I can sorta make the connections.

00:06:08.470 --> 00:06:09.470
Ta-da!

00:06:09.470 --> 00:06:10.970
Hidamari Apartments!

00:06:10.970 --> 00:06:12.470
Wow!

00:06:12.470 --> 00:06:15.650
You even drew in all the details!

00:06:15.650 --> 00:06:18.130
This is incredible, Miyako-senpai!

00:06:19.980 --> 00:06:22.730
Miya-chan, what is this?

00:06:22.730 --> 00:06:25.740
Don't look!

00:06:26.380 --> 00:06:29.610
I'm saving the surprise until someone reaches this square.

00:06:33.120 --> 00:06:37.430
We should use the occupations that we're likely to get, I guess.

00:06:37.430 --> 00:06:38.960
What could they be?

00:06:38.960 --> 00:06:42.030
Like designer or illustrator?

00:06:42.030 --> 00:06:43.040
A painter!

00:06:44.040 --> 00:06:46.530
Of course, a best-selling author.

00:06:46.530 --> 00:06:48.190
Jeez.

00:06:48.190 --> 00:06:50.430
Then, I'm writing down "art teacher."

00:06:50.430 --> 00:06:51.750
Prime Minister!

00:06:51.750 --> 00:06:53.250
That's supposed to be likely?

00:06:56.300 --> 00:06:58.750
I wish I had a dream career too.

00:06:58.750 --> 00:07:03.110
For us, they're mostly jobs that deal with art in one way or another.

00:07:03.110 --> 00:07:06.090
What do you want to become in the future?

00:07:06.090 --> 00:07:10.610
Well... I haven't thought about it at all.

00:07:10.610 --> 00:07:12.530
You're still a first-year.

00:07:12.530 --> 00:07:14.510
I'm sure most people decide much later.

00:07:14.510 --> 00:07:17.370
I hope you find a wonderful dream.

00:07:17.370 --> 00:07:18.290
Thanks!

00:07:22.860 --> 00:07:25.650
What kind of event grids are you making, Nazuna?

00:07:25.650 --> 00:07:27.590
U-Um...

00:07:28.180 --> 00:07:34.550
Whoever lands on this square has to massage the person sitting to the left until her next turn.

00:07:34.550 --> 00:07:40.910
Whoever lands on this square has to end her sentences with "meow" until the next turn.

00:07:41.620 --> 00:07:44.390
The game is about the amount of money you have.

00:07:44.390 --> 00:07:46.940
These have nothing to do with money.

00:07:50.780 --> 00:07:52.390
Finished!

00:07:53.110 --> 00:07:58.870
All right, let's go get the landlady and get start—

00:07:58.870 --> 00:08:01.830
We should eat before we start playing.

00:08:01.830 --> 00:08:03.120
Good idea!

00:08:03.120 --> 00:08:06.210
Okay, I'll go make some rice balls.

00:08:06.210 --> 00:08:07.250
I'll help.

00:08:07.250 --> 00:08:09.880
I... I'll make miso soup!

00:08:09.880 --> 00:08:10.800
Ooh!

00:08:10.800 --> 00:08:12.570
Nazuna, do you think you can handle it?

00:08:12.570 --> 00:08:14.250
Yeah, I'm gonna try.

00:08:14.250 --> 00:08:16.070
Nori-chan, can you come with me in case I need help?

00:08:16.070 --> 00:08:17.060
Sure.

00:08:17.060 --> 00:08:21.310
Yuno, Miyako, set the table and wake up the landlady, okay?

00:08:21.310 --> 00:08:23.060
Aye aye, sir.

00:08:25.060 --> 00:08:26.810
Bon appétit!

00:08:27.570 --> 00:08:28.850
This is good!

00:08:28.850 --> 00:08:31.210
It's got just the right amount of salt!

00:08:31.210 --> 00:08:35.160
Yeah, I can taste the warmth of Hiro-san's palm...

00:08:35.160 --> 00:08:36.930
Then you don't have to eat it!

00:08:36.930 --> 00:08:39.670
I was trying to <i>compliment</i> you!

00:08:39.670 --> 00:08:43.040
It didn't sound like it!

00:08:44.500 --> 00:08:48.110
Nazuna-chan's miso soup is good too!

00:08:48.110 --> 00:08:49.390
You're right.

00:08:49.390 --> 00:08:51.110
I think you've improved.

00:08:52.130 --> 00:08:55.590
It was unnerving to watch her make it, though.

00:08:56.120 --> 00:08:58.930
I can handle miso soup now!

00:08:59.620 --> 00:09:00.790
It's good!

00:09:01.270 --> 00:09:04.690
Nazuna-chan, this miso soup is good.

00:09:04.690 --> 00:09:06.520
It's good, but...

00:09:07.520 --> 00:09:09.730
Isn't there way too much tofu?

00:09:10.480 --> 00:09:13.990
U-Um, the store was having a sale the other day...

00:09:13.990 --> 00:09:17.850
I bought a whole bunch, but then I realized they were expiring today.

00:09:17.850 --> 00:09:19.490
So they were all...

00:09:20.240 --> 00:09:21.310
Oh, yeah.

00:09:21.310 --> 00:09:23.690
Tofu tends to rot quickly, after all.

00:09:23.690 --> 00:09:24.750
Yeah!

00:09:24.750 --> 00:09:26.250
Tofu...

00:09:26.250 --> 00:09:28.450
trots quickly?

00:09:33.010 --> 00:09:36.000
Oh, this is well done!

00:09:36.850 --> 00:09:39.050
It starts with you moving into Hidamari Apartments?

00:09:39.220 --> 00:09:42.110
And the goal is to become the owner?

00:09:43.020 --> 00:09:45.560
That's the last goal, the billionaire!

00:09:45.560 --> 00:09:50.280
The owner of Hidamari Apartments is far from a billionaire.

00:09:50.590 --> 00:09:51.580
Well, whatever.

00:09:51.580 --> 00:09:52.760
Let's get started!

00:09:52.760 --> 00:09:56.870
Huh? This game is for two to six people.

00:09:59.290 --> 00:10:00.370
Okay.

00:10:00.370 --> 00:10:02.630
Nazuna-chan!

00:10:02.630 --> 00:10:04.680
Let's team up.

00:10:03.710 --> 00:10:05.710
Why me?!

00:10:06.460 --> 00:10:08.280
Team Regular.

00:10:08.280 --> 00:10:11.970
The word "regular" isn't really how I'd describe you.

00:10:11.970 --> 00:10:16.350
Okay, from entering Hidamari Apartments and Yamabuki High School...

00:10:16.350 --> 00:10:18.180
Begin!

00:10:19.180 --> 00:10:20.180
One!

00:10:20.180 --> 00:10:22.440
"Matriculation and welcome ceremonies"...

00:10:22.440 --> 00:10:25.190
I can get $1000 from everyone!

00:10:26.190 --> 00:10:29.420
But we're in the same year!

00:10:29.420 --> 00:10:32.200
Miya-chan, this is how the game works.

00:10:35.580 --> 00:10:36.830
Let's see...

00:10:36.830 --> 00:10:39.830
"The Yamabuki Jizou gets in the way.

00:10:39.830 --> 00:10:41.580
Skip next turn...?"

00:10:41.580 --> 00:10:44.160
What's the Yamabuki Jizou?

00:10:44.160 --> 00:10:46.440
Oh, you haven't seen it?

00:10:46.440 --> 00:10:50.520
Deep inside the bamboo thicket next to Yamabuki High's tennis courts,

00:10:50.520 --> 00:10:52.130
there's a Jizou statue.

00:10:52.130 --> 00:10:53.380
Wow!

00:10:53.380 --> 00:10:57.440
You can pray to the statue to make your breasts bigger.

00:10:57.440 --> 00:10:59.000
Y-You can?

00:10:59.000 --> 00:11:01.000
Sae, that's it!

00:11:01.000 --> 00:11:03.160
Pleading to a divine being is your only chance now.

00:11:03.160 --> 00:11:04.650
What are you implying?!

00:11:04.650 --> 00:11:08.980
I realized a long time that it wouldn't help.

00:11:13.110 --> 00:11:15.450
Three, four, five.

00:11:15.450 --> 00:11:16.660
What do we have here?

00:11:16.660 --> 00:11:20.700
"Chinese fair, eat crab fried rice at the cafeteria.

00:11:21.010 --> 00:11:22.520
Pay $1,000."

00:11:22.520 --> 00:11:23.060
Here.

00:11:23.060 --> 00:11:23.960
Thanks!

00:11:23.960 --> 00:11:24.800
Spin!

00:11:26.080 --> 00:11:27.460
I...

00:11:27.460 --> 00:11:30.210
"go to Masanoyu Bathhouse with everyone...

00:11:30.210 --> 00:11:31.460
and pay $1,000."

00:11:31.460 --> 00:11:33.050
I'll be taking that.

00:11:34.050 --> 00:11:36.760
Yunocchi, that's expensive!

00:11:36.760 --> 00:11:39.890
A thousand is the smallest denomination we have...

00:11:44.270 --> 00:11:46.900
"Win a seafood gift set."

00:11:46.900 --> 00:11:48.860
And I get $100000.

00:11:49.890 --> 00:11:51.160
That's a lot of money!

00:11:51.160 --> 00:11:52.780
What is this?

00:11:52.780 --> 00:11:57.020
It means you're a hyper lucky girl, Norippe.

00:11:59.410 --> 00:12:00.910
One, two...

00:12:01.740 --> 00:12:06.000
"Whoever lands on this square has to end her sentences with 'meow'

00:12:06.000 --> 00:12:08.250
until the next turn."

00:12:08.250 --> 00:12:10.980
Congrats, Sae-san!

00:12:10.980 --> 00:12:13.120
I won't speak!

00:12:13.120 --> 00:12:15.380
What? That's no fun.

00:12:17.710 --> 00:12:19.100
It's from Chika-chan.

00:12:19.100 --> 00:12:19.890
You're right!

00:12:19.890 --> 00:12:21.010
Chika?

00:12:21.010 --> 00:12:22.390
Sae!

00:12:24.640 --> 00:12:26.390
Hello, Chika-chan?

00:12:26.390 --> 00:12:28.620
Oh, is that you, Yuno-san?

00:12:28.620 --> 00:12:30.300
It's been a while!

00:12:30.300 --> 00:12:32.940
How's it going? Is your Life looking good?

00:12:32.940 --> 00:12:35.320
Huh? How did you know?

00:12:35.320 --> 00:12:39.570
Nori messaged me and told me you guys were playing the Game of Life Experience.

00:12:40.570 --> 00:12:41.950
Chika-chan!

00:12:42.750 --> 00:12:44.280
I hear Miyako-san!

00:12:44.280 --> 00:12:45.820
How's she doing?

00:12:45.820 --> 00:12:48.140
Everyone's doing great!

00:12:48.140 --> 00:12:49.330
How about you, Chika-chan?

00:12:49.730 --> 00:12:51.220
I'm doing just fine,

00:12:51.220 --> 00:12:53.990
but I've been busy with my club activities.

00:12:53.990 --> 00:12:57.980
I get stuck with a lot of chores because I'm a first-year.

00:12:55.450 --> 00:12:56.520
Who's that?

00:12:56.520 --> 00:12:58.460
Sae-san's little sister.

00:12:58.460 --> 00:12:59.340
Oh!

00:13:00.340 --> 00:13:03.200
Then she should speak with her big sister too!

00:13:03.200 --> 00:13:06.180
Hey, your big sister wants to talk to you!

00:13:06.790 --> 00:13:07.600
Who's that?

00:13:07.600 --> 00:13:08.440
Um...

00:13:08.440 --> 00:13:10.690
Is Onee-chan going to talk to me?

00:13:15.770 --> 00:13:17.000
Onee-chan?

00:13:17.000 --> 00:13:18.950
Is that you?

00:13:20.450 --> 00:13:22.700
Yeah, it's me...

00:13:22.700 --> 00:13:23.700
Meow.

00:13:24.450 --> 00:13:25.950
Huh? What was that?

00:13:25.950 --> 00:13:28.160
It's me now, meow.

00:13:28.160 --> 00:13:31.790
We're in the middle of the game, so I'm hanging up, meow.

00:13:34.430 --> 00:13:36.540
What on Earth are you doing?

00:13:36.540 --> 00:13:38.760
Is that some kind of penalty?

00:13:38.760 --> 00:13:40.340
That must be embarrassing!

00:13:40.340 --> 00:13:42.540
Meow! Like a cat!

00:13:43.470 --> 00:13:45.100
Shut up!

00:13:45.100 --> 00:13:45.940
...meow.

00:13:45.940 --> 00:13:47.980
Remember this!

00:13:47.980 --> 00:13:48.730
...meow.

00:13:50.590 --> 00:13:54.800
Onee-chan, you don't sound threatening at all!

00:13:54.800 --> 00:13:57.440
Well, I don't want to hold you up for too long,

00:13:57.440 --> 00:13:58.740
so I'm hanging up, meow!

00:13:59.990 --> 00:14:01.490
Chika!

00:14:02.370 --> 00:14:04.870
For crying out loud, Chika!

00:14:04.870 --> 00:14:06.120
...meow.

00:14:07.580 --> 00:14:11.920
I didn't expect her timing to be so perfect!

00:14:11.920 --> 00:14:14.500
Maybe she could tell from her sixth sense.

00:14:16.670 --> 00:14:18.260
You all know her, huh?

00:14:18.260 --> 00:14:21.860
Yeah, she came over here a few times.

00:14:21.860 --> 00:14:24.890
She's a first-year in high school, just like us.

00:14:24.890 --> 00:14:26.760
You're really close friends!

00:14:26.760 --> 00:14:30.220
No wonder you're good at taking care of others, Sae.

00:14:30.220 --> 00:14:32.500
Not at all... meow.

00:14:33.270 --> 00:14:35.120
You're so cute!

00:14:39.400 --> 00:14:42.580
"Your caterpillar grew wings and became a moth.

00:14:42.580 --> 00:14:44.410
Due to the shock, you go back three squares."

00:14:44.410 --> 00:14:46.300
What? A moth?

00:14:46.300 --> 00:14:48.580
I made that square!

00:14:48.580 --> 00:14:51.500
Oh yeah, I remember that happening.

00:14:51.500 --> 00:14:56.000
Last year, Yunocchi grew a caterpillar thinking it'd become a butterfly,

00:14:56.000 --> 00:14:58.720
but it turned out to be a moth when it grew wings.

00:14:58.720 --> 00:15:01.670
We were running all over the place trying to get it out of the room!

00:15:01.670 --> 00:15:03.670
That'd be quite a shock indeed.

00:15:03.670 --> 00:15:06.260
I'm a little hungry.

00:15:06.260 --> 00:15:09.320
Yuno-chan, got any beer?

00:15:09.320 --> 00:15:11.950
Sorry, but I don't have beer.

00:15:11.950 --> 00:15:14.760
She's a minor! Why would she have any?!

00:15:14.760 --> 00:15:15.770
It was worth a shot.

00:15:15.770 --> 00:15:18.610
Oh, I have some snacks.

00:15:18.610 --> 00:15:20.610
Mild tuna flavor...

00:15:20.610 --> 00:15:24.860
Yuno-chan, that makes me crave for beer even more!

00:15:28.990 --> 00:15:31.000
One, two, three.

00:15:31.000 --> 00:15:32.000
You won the Monthly Kirara Prize!

00:15:31.000 --> 00:15:32.000
You've become a bestselling author.

00:15:32.000 --> 00:15:33.080
Awesome!

00:15:33.850 --> 00:15:36.670
I've become a bestselling author!

00:15:37.000 --> 00:15:38.700
So you got that one, huh?

00:15:38.700 --> 00:15:40.050
I'm a painter.

00:15:40.380 --> 00:15:42.920
I've become an art teacher!

00:15:43.260 --> 00:15:45.050
I'm a designer!

00:15:45.380 --> 00:15:48.850
I... I became the Prime Minister!

00:15:50.680 --> 00:15:54.620
Prime Minister, you need to raise employment rates!

00:15:54.620 --> 00:15:57.440
Wh-What am I supposed to do?

00:15:57.440 --> 00:15:59.860
When I was in high school,

00:15:59.860 --> 00:16:03.740
I didn't even think I'd become a landlady when I grew up.

00:16:03.740 --> 00:16:05.300
Really?

00:16:05.300 --> 00:16:06.980
Well, no one does.

00:16:06.980 --> 00:16:10.520
What did you want to become when you were in high school?

00:16:10.520 --> 00:16:12.500
I can't tell you that.

00:16:12.500 --> 00:16:14.500
That's a profound smile.

00:16:14.500 --> 00:16:16.340
You're all still young.

00:16:16.340 --> 00:16:18.160
You can become anything!

00:16:18.160 --> 00:16:21.750
Don't worry too much and just chase after a grand dream!

00:16:21.750 --> 00:16:24.480
You're young too!

00:16:24.480 --> 00:16:26.240
You can still pursue your dreams and—

00:16:26.240 --> 00:16:27.000
T-Time out.

00:16:27.000 --> 00:16:29.260
I can't do that anymore.

00:16:29.260 --> 00:16:30.510
Your dreams...

00:16:31.510 --> 00:16:34.770
What's your job, Landlady?

00:16:37.270 --> 00:16:39.080
Now that I think about it...

00:16:39.080 --> 00:16:40.680
What do you mean?

00:16:40.680 --> 00:16:42.400
I'm the landlady of Hidamari Apartments.

00:16:42.400 --> 00:16:45.690
You don't actually come here that often.

00:16:45.690 --> 00:16:47.700
What do you do the rest of the time?

00:16:47.700 --> 00:16:50.700
I occasionally see you working part-time, but...

00:16:50.700 --> 00:16:54.830
When did you become the owner of Hidamari Apartments?

00:16:57.330 --> 00:17:00.720
When you're an adult, life can throw a lot of things your way.

00:17:00.720 --> 00:17:02.920
The more secrets you have,

00:17:02.920 --> 00:17:05.090
the more mysterious and attractive you come across as!

00:17:10.390 --> 00:17:15.140
"You give birth to twins. As congratulations, you get $2000 from everyone."

00:17:15.140 --> 00:17:17.700
Geez, twins are kind of...

00:17:17.700 --> 00:17:18.960
Sae!

00:17:18.960 --> 00:17:20.420
It's cause for celebration.

00:17:20.420 --> 00:17:22.100
Don't complain.

00:17:22.100 --> 00:17:22.900
There you go!

00:17:22.900 --> 00:17:25.100
Sae-san, congratulations!

00:17:25.100 --> 00:17:27.200
You're fighting the declining birth rates!

00:17:27.200 --> 00:17:28.650
Come on.

00:17:31.990 --> 00:17:34.910
It's like Chinese acrobatics!

00:17:36.540 --> 00:17:40.040
"Haircut at the Olive, pay $4,000."

00:17:40.040 --> 00:17:43.700
Let's see, $4,000, $4,000...

00:17:44.340 --> 00:17:46.210
Come on, Sae.

00:17:46.210 --> 00:17:49.800
You're so slow because you don't sort your bills.

00:17:51.800 --> 00:17:52.840
There!

00:17:52.840 --> 00:17:54.140
Wow, that's neat!

00:17:54.140 --> 00:17:54.940
Thanks.

00:17:54.940 --> 00:17:56.310
You're welcome.

00:17:56.310 --> 00:17:59.440
Do you want me to count them all?

00:17:59.440 --> 00:18:01.810
Would you? Thanks.

00:18:01.810 --> 00:18:05.320
Then, I'll pay you $3,000 for managing my funds.

00:18:05.320 --> 00:18:08.240
That's not a rule violation, right, Prime Minister?

00:18:08.240 --> 00:18:09.240
It's fine.

00:18:09.240 --> 00:18:11.320
These are some pretty loose rules.

00:18:17.330 --> 00:18:19.200
Now, time to announce the results.

00:18:20.710 --> 00:18:24.960
With a total amount of $832,000, the winner is...

00:18:25.710 --> 00:18:27.710
Nori!

00:18:27.710 --> 00:18:29.170
Yay!

00:18:29.170 --> 00:18:34.800
Nori was a freeter, so did she get more money than the Prime Minister?

00:18:34.800 --> 00:18:39.180
Probably because of a bunch of high-revenue events I got.

00:18:41.940 --> 00:18:47.180
Maybe we shouldn't have ruined the balance of a game put together by professionals after all.

00:18:47.180 --> 00:18:48.640
Probably.

00:18:50.440 --> 00:18:56.280
First off, I think your Game of Life Experience has too few grids where you pay money.

00:18:56.280 --> 00:18:59.340
Maybe it's because we added a lot of good grids.

00:18:59.340 --> 00:19:02.670
Yeah, we were thinking about our future and all.

00:19:12.170 --> 00:19:15.580
Well, that was a lot of fun, surprisingly.

00:19:15.580 --> 00:19:17.100
Glad to hear it.

00:19:18.750 --> 00:19:21.350
You're shining.

00:19:21.350 --> 00:19:22.610
Huh?

00:19:22.610 --> 00:19:25.980
Our lives will be smooth sailing!

00:19:25.980 --> 00:19:27.840
I'm sure they will.

00:19:29.110 --> 00:19:32.910
Man, I envy your youth!

00:19:32.910 --> 00:19:34.990
I can't keep up with your energy.

00:19:34.990 --> 00:19:37.740
You're young too!

00:19:37.740 --> 00:19:42.460
I'm sure you can be more energetic...

00:19:39.440 --> 00:19:42.460
I already told you to cut it out.

00:19:44.000 --> 00:19:45.500
See you, then.

00:19:45.500 --> 00:19:47.500
Good-bye!

00:19:50.000 --> 00:19:53.180
These are the signs you made, right?

00:19:53.180 --> 00:19:54.460
Yeah.

00:19:54.460 --> 00:19:55.580
They're wonderful.

00:19:55.580 --> 00:19:56.560
You think so?

00:19:56.560 --> 00:19:59.320
I had a lot of fun today!

00:19:59.320 --> 00:20:01.900
I got to hear some new stories about you.

00:20:01.900 --> 00:20:03.840
There's more where those came from.

00:20:03.840 --> 00:20:07.860
Hiro-san had a huge box of diet jelly—

00:20:08.860 --> 00:20:10.640
Never mind what she said.

00:20:12.110 --> 00:20:15.520
We should make a lot of good memories here too.

00:20:15.520 --> 00:20:16.200
Yeah!

00:20:18.950 --> 00:20:19.950
Look!

00:20:19.950 --> 00:20:21.450
The first star of the night!

00:20:21.450 --> 00:20:23.700
There you are!

00:20:24.270 --> 00:20:25.710
There you are!

00:20:29.460 --> 00:20:30.710
Oh yeah.

00:20:30.710 --> 00:20:33.710
No one landed on this square.

00:20:36.970 --> 00:20:38.740
Sympathy money...

00:20:38.740 --> 00:20:40.970
I guess that's still money won.

00:20:42.930 --> 00:20:44.350
Hey, Yunocchi!

00:20:44.350 --> 00:20:50.440
Let's keep this Hidamari edition of the Game of Life Experience around <i>forever</i>!

00:20:50.860 --> 00:20:56.560
If the girls who come to live at Hidamari Apartments keep improving it,

00:20:56.560 --> 00:21:03.540
it'll keep piling up and in a couple of decades it'll be an amazing game!

00:21:03.540 --> 00:21:05.040
Yeah.

00:21:05.040 --> 00:21:08.700
And hopefully we'll get together and play again.

00:21:10.290 --> 00:21:12.880
We ended up playing all day.

00:21:12.880 --> 00:21:15.670
Yeah, but I feel re-energized now.

00:21:15.670 --> 00:21:18.760
Let's hit the books hard for our college entrance exams tomorrow.

00:21:18.760 --> 00:21:20.010
Yep!

00:21:23.010 --> 00:21:27.100
The upperclassmen cleaned this room for us, didn't they?

00:21:27.100 --> 00:21:31.360
I wonder what I'll do for the underclassmen when I'm older.

00:21:32.830 --> 00:21:36.120
I wonder what I'll become in the future.

00:21:36.890 --> 00:21:41.000
As Sae-san said, we can take our time thinking about it.

00:21:41.000 --> 00:21:44.160
One of us could even become the Prime Minister if we aimed for it now!

00:21:44.160 --> 00:21:44.790
What?

00:21:44.790 --> 00:21:47.920
But you're a scatterbrain, so maybe not.

00:21:47.920 --> 00:21:49.940
Nori-chan, that's mean!

00:21:49.940 --> 00:21:51.440
I'm just kidding.

00:22:01.170 --> 00:22:04.600
One, two, three!

00:22:07.790 --> 00:22:08.980
Splash!

00:22:11.540 --> 00:22:13.900
Give me a haiku about Hidamari Apartments!

00:22:13.900 --> 00:22:15.120
Oh, Hidamari!

00:22:15.120 --> 00:22:16.420
Even on rainy days,

00:22:16.420 --> 00:22:17.600
Hidamari Apartments!

00:22:17.600 --> 00:22:19.640
Well, that's not too great.

00:22:19.640 --> 00:22:21.780
Um, how about snow?

00:22:21.780 --> 00:22:22.720
That might be nice.

00:22:22.720 --> 00:22:24.080
Then let's try again.

00:22:24.080 --> 00:22:25.480
Oh, Hidamari!

00:22:25.480 --> 00:22:26.780
When it's snowy outside,

00:22:26.780 --> 00:22:28.360
we don't leave the kotatsu!

00:22:28.360 --> 00:22:30.500
So cozy!

00:22:30.500 --> 00:22:33.940
Next time: "December 2nd, An Educational Snowball Fight,"

00:22:33.940 --> 00:22:36.840
"December 15th, Hidamari Cheer Team."

00:22:36.840 --> 00:22:40.200
We'll be waiting at Hidamari Apartments, so come visit us!
